{"sections":[],"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre-Native-for-iOS\/Tile_URL_Templates","interfaceLanguage":"occ"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"MapLibre"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Tile URL Templates"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNTileSource"},{"type":"text","text":" objects, specifically "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNRasterTileSource"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNVectorTileSource"},{"type":"text","text":" objects, can be created using an initializer that accepts"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an array of tile URL templates. Tile URL templates are strings that specify the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"URLs of the vector tiles or raster tile images to load. A template resembles an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"absolute URL, but with any number of placeholder strings that the source"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"evaluates based on the tile it needs to load. For example:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"http:\/\/www.example.com\/tiles\/{z}\/{x}\/{y}.pbf","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" could be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"evaluated as "},{"code":"http:\/\/www.example.com\/tiles\/14\/6\/9.pbf","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"http:\/\/www.example.com\/tiles\/{z}\/{x}\/{y}{ratio}.png","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" could be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"evaluated as "},{"code":"http:\/\/www.example.com\/tiles\/14\/6\/9@2x.png","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Tile URL templates are also used to define tilesets in TileJSON manifests or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/maplibre.org\/maplibre-style-spec\/sources\/#raster","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/maplibre.org\/maplibre-style-spec\/sources\/#vector-tiles","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sources in style JSON files. See the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/mapbox\/tilejson-spec\/tree\/master\/2.2.0","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for information about tile URL templates in the context of a TileJSON or style"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"JSON file."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Tile sources support the following placeholder strings in tile URL templates,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"all of which are optional:"}]},{"header":"row","type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Placeholder string"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Description"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"{x}","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The index of the tile along the map’s x axis according to Spherical Mercator projection. If the value is 0, the tile’s left edge corresponds to the 180th meridian west. If the value is 2^z−1, the tile’s right edge corresponds to the 180th meridian east."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"{y}","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The index of the tile along the map’s y axis according to Spherical Mercator projection. If the value is 0, the tile’s tile edge corresponds to arctan(sinh(π)), or approximately 85.0511 degrees north. If the value is 2^z−1, the tile’s bottom edge corresponds to −arctan(sinh(π)), or approximately 85.0511 degrees south. The y axis is inverted if the options parameter contains "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNTileSourceOptionTileCoordinateSystem"},{"type":"text","text":" with a value of "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNTileCoordinateSystem\/MLNTileCoordinateSystemTMS"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"{z}","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The tile’s zoom level. At zoom level 0, each tile covers the entire world map; at zoom level 1, it covers ¼ of the world; at zoom level 2, 1⁄16 of the world, and so on. For tiles loaded by a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNRasterTileSource"},{"type":"text","text":" object, whether the tile zoom level matches the map’s current zoom level depends on the value of the source’s tile size as specified in the "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNTileSourceOptionTileSize"},{"type":"text","text":" key of the options parameter."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"{bbox-epsg-3857}","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The tile’s bounding box, expressed as a comma-separated list of the tile’s western, southern, eastern, and northern extents according to Spherical Mercator (EPSG:3857) projection. The bounding box is typically used with map services conforming to the "},{"type":"text","text":"Web Map Service"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"{quadkey}","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A quadkey indicating both the tile’s location and its zoom level. The quadkey is typically used with "},{"type":"text","text":"Bing Maps"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"{ratio}","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A suffix indicating the resolution of the tile image. The suffix is the empty string for standard resolution displays and "},{"code":"@2x","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for Retina displays, including displays for which "},{"code":"UIScreen.scale","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is 3."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"{prefix}","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Two hexadecimal digits chosen such that each visible tile has a different prefix. The prefix is typically used for domain sharding."}]}]]]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For more information about the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{x}"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{y}"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{z}"},{"type":"text","text":" placeholder strings,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"consult the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/wiki.openstreetmap.org\/wiki\/Slippy_map_tilenames"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"occ"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/maplibre-native-for-ios\/tile_url_templates"]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Other Articles","identifiers":["doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre-Native-for-iOS\/Customizin